dsmr-qmail-run (1.0-10) trixie; urgency=low

  * qmail-smtpd/run, qmail-submission/run: select the recipient validation
    gate at exec time.  When /var/qmail/bin/localfirst-rcptcheck exists
    (provided by dsmr-localfirst) it becomes the sole RCPTCHECK gate and
    chkuser is left off, so system-user recipients on hybrid domains are
    accepted at SMTP time; the validator chains to the outbound overlimit
    throttle on accept.  When the bridge is absent, chkuser plus the standalone
    overlimit throttle are used exactly as before.  Backwards-compatible.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

dsmr-qmail-run (1.0-9) trixie; urgency=low

  * qmail-submission/run: select SMTP-AUTH backend at exec time.
    When /var/qmail/bin/checkpassword-dovecot exists (provided by
    dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot) the bridge is used, routing AUTH through
    dovecot's chained passdbs so vpopmail virtual users and curated system
    users authenticate from one source.  When the bridge is absent, falls
    back to vchkpw, preserving prior behaviour.  Backwards-compatible.

