dsmr-qmail-run (1.0-4) trixie; urgency=high

  * qmail-smtpd/run: do not set ENABLE_SPP=0 when SPP is not configured.
    The qmail-spp patch treats any presence of ENABLE_SPP (including "0" and
    empty string) as a trigger to initialise SPP, reading the smtpplugins
    control file.  When that file is absent, qmail-smtpd exits immediately
    with "421 unable to read controls", rejecting every inbound connection on
    port 25.  Fix: only export ENABLE_SPP=1 when smtpplugins + plugins dir
    both exist; leave the variable unset otherwise.

 -- Brian O'Reilly <fade@deepsky.com>  Sat, 04 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0400

